course: dictionary
lesson: 1592
title: Cheater: breaking the rules in secret
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A cheater is a person who cheats. Cheating means breaking the rules in secret to win or to get something you should not have. Cheat is the action, and cheater is the person who does it.
explain: The word can also mean someone who is not faithful or honest with a partner or friend. Read the words around it: «Not every brilliant player is a cheater, though.» The word «though» shows that a brilliant player might be suspected, but being very good does not make someone a cheater.
explain: Look for clues in games, sport and tests: copying answers, peeking, changing the score or ignoring the rules are what cheaters do. Always swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: A cheater is a person who breaks the rules secretly to win.
fact: «Cheater» can also mean someone who is not honest or faithful to a partner or friend.
fact: The seven letters of TEACHER also make «CHEATER» and «HECTARE», so the same letters can spell different words.
fact: «Cheaters never prosper» is a saying that means people who cheat do not succeed in the end.
exercise: What is a cheater, in a game? | A person who reads the rules out loud | A person who is very fast at running | A person who lost the game | *A person who breaks the rules secretly to win
exercise: Which word is made from the same seven letters as TEACHER? | heart | cheat | *CHEATER | reach
exercise: «Not every brilliant player is a cheater, though.» What does the word though tell you? | Players never cheat at all | *A brilliant player is not automatically a cheater | Brilliant players are always cheaters | Cheaters are always brilliant players
test: What does cheater mean when someone lies to their best friend? | Someone who runs very fast | Someone who loves reading books | *Someone who is not honest with a friend | Someone who is very kind and helpful
test: «Games have a report button for cheaters, and reports are checked.» What does this tell you? | Cheaters are given a prize | Cheaters cannot play games at all | Reports are never read | *Players can report cheaters, and the reports are looked at
exam: Which one describes a cheater in a test? | Someone who asks the teacher for help | *Someone who copies answers in secret | Someone who finishes first and says so | Someone who follows every rule and works alone
